@startuml
title Initiated built-in test - detailed

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 105

actor User
boundary "USB terminal" as Terminal
control "Foreground loop / UI" as UI
control "IBIT state machine" as IBIT
participant "RP2354 peripherals" as MCU
database "Boot flash" as Flash
database "QSPI PSRAM" as PSRAM
participant "Trion FPGA" as FPGA
participant "RGB LED / SW1" as Panel
participant Watchdog as WD

User -> Terminal : Press any key during the repeating banner
Terminal -> UI : Character
UI -> Terminal : Draw menu
User -> Terminal : Press 1
Terminal -> UI : Select full built-in test
UI -> UI : Release diagnostics heartbeat ownership of LED
UI -> IBIT : start(); reset phase, tally and cached memory sample
IBIT -> Terminal : "Initiated built-in test"

note over UI, WD
  Every foreground pass still runs diagnostics first,
  feeding the watchdog before USB service and IBIT polling.
  At most one completed IBIT step is reported per pass.
end note

group Steps 1-5 - MCU identity and configuration facts
  IBIT -> MCU : 1. Read cached SYSINFO chip identity
  MCU --> IBIT : Manufacturer, part, revision, architecture, cores
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL Chip identity
  IBIT -> MCU : 2. Read cached 64-bit flash unique ID
  MCU --> IBIT : Unique ID
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL Board identity
  IBIT -> MCU : 3. Measure clk_sys and clk_usb
  MCU --> IBIT : Frequencies and configured reference clock
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL Clocks (1 percent tolerance)
  IBIT -> MCU : 4. Read linked flash and SRAM sizes
  MCU --> IBIT : 2048 KiB flash; 520 KiB SRAM expected
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL Memory sizing
  IBIT -> MCU : 5. Read cached OTP FLASH_DEVINFO size codes
  MCU --> IBIT : CS0 and CS1 codes
  IBIT -> Terminal : INFO only - values are not used for sizing
end

group Steps 6-7 - memories sharing SCLK and SD0..SD3
  IBIT -> MCU : BSP_MemoryCheck() once for this run
  MCU -> Flash : Read reset vectors through the uncached alias
  Flash --> MCU : Stack pointer and reset vector
  MCU -> PSRAM : Write/read three uncached probe words at first, middle and last
  PSRAM --> MCU : Probe readback
  MCU --> IBIT : One cached memory report used by both steps
  IBIT -> Terminal : 6. PASS/FAIL Boot flash

  IBIT -> MCU : Read cached boot-only PSRAM identity
  loop Full 2 MiB moving-inversion sweep, one chunk per foreground pass
    IBIT -> PSRAM : Mapped uncached write or verify operation
    PSRAM --> IBIT : Read data for verification
  end
  note over IBIT, PSRAM
    IBIT does not reset PSRAM or issue Read-ID.
    It uses the ordinary mapped-QPI window.
  end note
  IBIT -> Terminal : 7. PASS/FAIL QSPI PSRAM
end

group Steps 8-10 - board services
  IBIT -> MCU : 8. Sample on-die ADC temperature
  MCU --> IBIT : Raw ADC and milli-degrees C
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL range -20 C to +85 C

  IBIT -> MCU : 9. Capture USB health and frame number
  IBIT -> IBIT : Yield until at least 20 ms elapsed
  IBIT -> MCU : Capture USB health again
  MCU --> IBIT : DTR, suspend, SOF movement, TX space
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL USB link

  IBIT -> WD : 10. Write self-test marker and read it back
  WD --> IBIT : Marker value
  IBIT -> WD : Restore marker=IBIT
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL marker and previous boot reason
end

group Step 11 - establish FPGA reachability
  FPGA --> IBIT : Dedicated CDONE and STATUS pin levels
  IBIT -> FPGA : PING 0x9F
  FPGA --> IBIT : Design ID
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS only for CDONE high and ID 0xB8
end

group Steps 12-15 - each checks CDONE and PING before it begins
  loop Before each FPGA-dependent step
    FPGA --> IBIT : CDONE level
    IBIT -> FPGA : PING 0x9F
    FPGA --> IBIT : Design ID
    alt CDONE low or ID is not 0xB8
      IBIT -> Terminal : SKIP - FPGA not responding
    else FPGA reachable
      note over IBIT, FPGA : Run the selected dependent step below.
    end
  end

  IBIT -> FPGA : 12. Read status and save LED registers
  IBIT -> FPGA : Write 5A,A5,3C,C3 walking pattern
  FPGA --> IBIT : Read LED register values back
  IBIT -> FPGA : Restore saved LED registers
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL FPGA register bus

  loop 13. Red, green, blue, white and off phases
    IBIT -> FPGA : Write RGB/brightness/enable registers
    FPGA -> Panel : Drive PWM LED outputs
    FPGA --> IBIT : Register readback
    IBIT -> IBIT : Return PENDING until the next phase
  end
  IBIT -> FPGA : Restore pre-test LED state
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL RGB LED

  IBIT -> FPGA : 14. Clear button count and read baseline
  IBIT -> Terminal : Prompt to press SW1 within 15 s
  User -> Panel : Press SW1 (optional)
  Panel -> FPGA : Active-low button input
  FPGA -> FPGA : Debounce; latch event; increment saturating count
  loop Poll level and count every 50 ms
    IBIT -> FPGA : Read button level and count registers
    FPGA --> IBIT : Current level and count
  end
  alt Count changed before 15 s
    IBIT -> Terminal : PASS Button SW1
  else No press
    IBIT -> Terminal : TIMEOUT (not a hardware failure)
  end

  IBIT -> FPGA : 15. Latch and read 32-bit tick snapshot
  IBIT -> IBIT : Return PENDING for at least 500 ms
  IBIT -> FPGA : Latch and read second tick snapshot
  FPGA --> IBIT : Four byte-wide registers per snapshot
  IBIT -> Terminal : PASS/FAIL 32 MHz within 1 percent
end

alt Sequence reaches the final result
  IBIT -> Terminal : Print PASS/FAIL/TIMEOUT/SKIP/INFO totals and duration
else Any key arrives while activity is running
  User -> Terminal : Abort key
  Terminal -> UI : Character
  UI -> IBIT : stop(); restore saved LED state if necessary
  UI -> Terminal : "aborted"
end

UI -> UI : Reclaim diagnostics heartbeat LED
UI -> Terminal : Redraw menu

@enduml
